## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to plan robust, low-downtime testing for evolving data contracts in a multi-tenant real-time pipeline, ensuring no customer data loss or misinterpretation during schema changes.

## Key Concepts
- Avro schema evolution and compatibility modes (backward, forward, full)
- Schema Registry governance and canary rollouts
- End-to-end validation across data lake and dashboards
- Multi-tenant isolation and data drift detection
- Canary criteria and rollback triggers

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: publish with old and new schemas to Kafka
const avro = require('avsc');

// Validate compatibility before deployment
async function validateSchemaCompatibility(oldSchema, newSchema) {
  const registry = new SchemaRegistryClient();
  const isBackwardCompatible = await registry.testCompatibility(oldSchema, newSchema);
  const isForwardCompatible = await registry.testCompatibility(newSchema, oldSchema);

  return { isBackwardCompatible, isForwardCompatible };
}
```

